Subject: [PATCH] loc_core: create ASUS' LocApiV02 the way it expects

ASUS' libloc_api_v02.so refuses to create its LocApi when it is given a
MsgTask: createLocApiV02() returns NULL ("msgTask can not be NULL", logged when
the pointer is *not* NULL) and only builds the object, with a NULL MsgTask, when
it gets none. On stock that call never comes from libloc_core: liblbs_core.so,
the IZat proxy ContextBase asks first, creates the LocApi itself. Without the
IZat stack ContextBase fell through to a dummy LocApiBase and the GPS never
reached the modem.

So hand the getter NULL, and let LocApiBase take its context's MsgTask when it
is given none, which is what a LocApi built by an older blob ended up with. The
class layout is unchanged (checked against stock's libloc_core: same field
offsets), so the blob's inlined sendMsg() reads the right pointer.
---
--- a/core/ContextBase.cpp
+++ b/core/ContextBase.cpp
@@ -94,7 +94,7 @@
                 getLocApi_t* getter = (getLocApi_t*)dlsym(handle, "getLocApi");
                 if(getter != NULL) {
                     LOC_LOGD("%s:%d]: getter is not NULL for LocApiV02", __func__, __LINE__);
-                    locApi = (*getter)(mMsgTask, exMask, this);
+                    locApi = (*getter)(NULL, exMask, this);
                 }
             }
             // only RPC is the option now
--- a/core/LocApiBase.cpp
+++ b/core/LocApiBase.cpp
@@ -128,7 +128,8 @@
 LocApiBase::LocApiBase(const MsgTask* msgTask,
                        LOC_API_ADAPTER_EVENT_MASK_T excludedMask,
                        ContextBase* context) :
-    mExcludedMask(excludedMask), mMsgTask(msgTask),
+    mExcludedMask(excludedMask),
+    mMsgTask(msgTask != NULL || context == NULL ? msgTask : context->getMsgTask()),
     mMask(0), mSupportedMsg(0), mContext(context)
 {
     memset(mLocAdapters, 0, sizeof(mLocAdapters));
